# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Jing Wu et al. (2023). Universal interatomic potential for perovskite oxides.
#   Physical review. B./Physical review. B. doi:10.1103/physrevb.108.l180104  arXiv:2309.06391v3
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2309.06391v3 (sha256 6e387f73b2a9ebd7...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 436 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/wu2023.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the ABACUS PBEsol training database grown with DP-GEN
# from 3- to 6-element perovskite oxides (19,288 configurations), the
# DPA-1 model UniPero (DeePMD-kit; 6 A cutoff, two attention layers of
# 128 hidden dimensions, type embedding 8) and its MAEs on the training
# database. Task I/II test errors are given only as bounds; phase
# transitions and other properties are properties.

